---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
    <div
        data-home-lang="zh-hant"
        class="flex flex-col gap-4 lg:text-lg md:text-md w-full text-left dark:text-gray-100 transition-colors mt-3"
    >
        <p>
            Hi! Welcome to the colophon page. In here, I want to put something
            on how this page is being made.
        </p>
        <p class="lg:text-3xl md:text-2xl underline">Why a new version</p>
        <p>
            So actually, before this page, I have like, 3 different versions of
            my website. The 1st and 2nd version did not use any framework and is
            just a simple mix of HTML, CSS and JavaScript. However, A major
            disadvantage is that I cannot write blogs in md format. This is a
            bit tricky. Along that, old pages did not use any framework, and is
            somehow a great disadvantage for finding jobs.
        </p>
        <p>
            So we have the 3rd version of the page. It uses Astro.js as
            framework, the same as the current version. However, I procastinated
            a lot and did not put too much effort in maintaining that page due
            to the stress of finding jobs. The page looks rather incompleted,
            with no blog posts at all. With that website I totally lose
            motivation in making blogs.
        </p>
        <p>
            After I get a job, the idea of "completing" the website has arised.
            This at least includes adding different languages and also making a
            dark theme. Also, since the previous Astro.js version is developed
            based on a template, hence I have lot more limitations in developing
            to the way I love. So this is why I need a new version. Not only to
            build my favourite design, but also, a site that I would like to
            write things on.
        </p>
        <p class="lg:text-3xl md:text-2xl underline">How you designed this</p>
        So this website
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
